        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(transcript-stream): log stat/open errors instead of silently returning empty iterator",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n`streamSessionTranscriptLines` and `streamSessionTranscriptLinesReverse` used bare `catch { return; }` blocks that silently swallowed all filesystem errors. Replace them with `catch (err) { transcriptLog.warn(...); return; }`.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nIn `src/config/sessions/transcript-stream.ts`, both streaming functions catch `fs.promises.stat` / `fs.promises.open` errors and silently return empty iterators. While an empty iterator is the correct contract for missing files, other errors (permission denied, I/O error) should be visible in diagnostics.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe functions were designed to return an empty iterator when the file cannot be read, but the empty catch blocks discarded all diagnostic information.\n\n## Why This Fix\n\nSame pattern as [#84449](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/84449) and [#106385](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/106385) — `createSubsystemLogger` + `formatErrorMessage(err)`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Before**: EACCES error silently swallowed → empty iterator, no diagnostic\n- **After**: EACCES error logged → `[transcript-stream] Failed to stat transcript /root/nonexistent-transcript.jsonl: EACCES: permission denied`\n\n## Real Behavior Proof\n\n### Before (on main)\n```bash\n$ node --import tsx proof.mjs\nLines collected: 0\nFAIL: No warnings were emitted on stderr!\n```\n\n### After (with fix)\n```bash\n$ node --import tsx proof.mjs\nLines collected: 0\nPASS: Warning was emitted on stderr:\n  [transcript-stream] Failed to stat transcript /root/...: EACCES: permission denied\n```\n\n## Tests and Validation\n\n- `pnpm check` passed\n- Added regression test for permission error path\n",
